            <h2>Roboguard Perimeter Architecture & Specifications</h2>
            <p>Roboguard wireless outdoor perimeter sensors are premium, South African-designed early-warning intruder detection systems. Unlike traditional point-to-point active infrared beams that require precise alignment, Roboguard utilizes dual passive infrared (PIR) sensors to track heat and movement across a broad 110° arc, protecting roughly 400 square meters per unit.</p>

            <h3><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i> Key Technical Specifications & Coverage</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Detection Range & Arc:</strong> Detects motion up to 20 meters away across a wide 110° arc (covering 11 zones, one every 10 degrees).</li>
                <li><strong>Wireless Transmission:</strong> Transmits signals up to 400 meters line-of-sight back to the HQ base station (extendable up to 800 meters using compatible repeaters).</li>
                <li><strong>Power Architecture:</strong> Completely battery-operated using 8 x C-cell alkaline batteries per beam, delivering an exceptional service life of 3 to 5 years.</li>
                <li><strong>Lightning & Cabling Immunity:</strong> Because the beams are completely wireless and require zero physical trenching or cabling, they are entirely immune to lightning surges.</li>
                <li><strong>False Alarm Resistance:</strong> Built-in algorithm selectors and dual-sensor verification allow the system to ignore extreme weather, blowing foliage, and small animals.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3><i class="fas fa-tools"></i> Professional Installation & Deployment Methodology</h3>
            <p>Deploying Roboguard perimeter systems successfully relies on strategic placement and proper base station integration:</p>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Mounting Height & Angle:</strong> Mount sentry beams at a recommended height of 1 to 1.2 meters, pointing across potential entry paths rather than directly facing hot afternoon sun or reflective surfaces.</li>
                <li><strong>HQ Base Station Pairing:</strong> Connect the central Roboguard HQ Base to your primary home alarm panel or dedicated siren. A single HQ base can manage and monitor up to eight independent Roboguard beams.</li>
                <li><strong>Battery Maintenance & Testing:</strong> Monitor low-battery trouble flashes on the HQ base and replace C-cell batteries proactively every 3 to 5 years to maintain uninterrupted perimeter protection.</li>
            </ol>

            <div class="pro-tip-box">
                <h4><i class="fas fa-bolt"></i> Professional Integration Tip</h4>
                <p>Use the 4-button Roboguard remotes to arm and disarm perimeter zones independently while leaving your indoor alarm zones active or inactive according to your occupancy schedule.</p>
            </div>
